{"seq":41,"trial_id":"v04-cal-r3-2026-11/hermes-opus-gbrain-told-live-rr-l3-mu-v04-dev/rr-10-l3-quarrendon-ticket-retired/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T00:10:35.007Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-21T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"5f6363e16e097bf18b98ed8b78f752e1871adc7189bf028977dbbee34eb4417c","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV04CAL0001","text":"Hi Tobias, here's what I can find on Quarrendon Freight Lines (QFL) in places you can see. Note that I couldn't find any account files for QFL itself, like tickets or CRM.\n\nEau Claire gatehouse kiosk alerts:\n- A Moss note for Ruth dated 5 Oct 2025 says Thea Ramaswell opened ticket #PD-4492 on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers checking in by tablet for the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14 through 18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting their SMS bay assignments. Support patched the SMS gateway routing table at 19:30 that day. Thea confirmed the 04:00 shift on 5 Oct cleared the gate without any manual help. A follow-up was set to make sure the Eau Claire kiosk logs were archived before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window. I found nothing on whether that happened.\n- One caveat: this note shows up in the workspace knowledge base, but I couldn't open it in the shared files. Check it before you rely on it.\n\nBarcode scanners failing at Door 14:\n- The North team's QFL cheat sheet (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md, undated) says Thea logged ticket #4419. Gatehouse barcode scanners at Door 14 weren't reading trailer tags during third shift. The ticket was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing. I found no resolution recorded.\n- The ticket number conflicts with another file. Marcus Lindqvist's note from 14 Jul 2025 (members/marcus-lindqvist/notes/2025-07-14-marcus-q2-expansion-wrap.md) lists #4419 as \"Gate 3 printer lag\" (a BOL printout delay). It says a patch went out and is waiting for Thea to confirm. Check the ticket number with support before you put it in the file.\n\nAlso watch the name: Quarendon Freightways, with one r, is a different company. It isn't a Pemberline customer. Your July 2025 Tansleigh #88412 scanner thread in #central-team was about them, not QFL.\n\nQFL is a North team account (Dana Okafor owns it now). If you need something more current than these notes, Dana or Ilse Varga are the people to ask."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV04CAL0001","ts":"1792591200.000130"}}
